<title>POLAND: Poland's KGHM picks SocGen to lead $200 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Poland's KGHM picks SocGen to lead $200 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's KGHM Polska Miedz SA copper concern said in a statement on Wednesday it had awarded French bank Societe Generale a mandate to lead a syndicated loan for its development needs.</p>
<p>KGHM earlier said in its prospectus that it sought a $200 million syndicated loan to finance a part of its investment programme. KGHM has said it plans to invest a total of $800 million by the year 2001.</p>
<p>KGHM said in the statement it would sign a final loan agreement based on agreed preliminary conditions.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
